### 1. Product Manager (PM)
**Requirement Update:**
- **Feature:** Notification UI Enhancement.
- **User Story:** As a user, I want to see the most recent notifications at the top of the list so I don't have to scroll to find new updates.
- **Acceptance Criteria:**
    1. Notifications are sorted by `timestamp` in descending order (newest first).
    2. The "Clear All" button must be selectable via `data-testid="clear-all-btn"` for automated testing.

### 2. Solution Architect (SA)
**Technical Assessment:**
- **Target File:** `src/components/NotificationsList.tsx` (assuming standard project structure).
- **Logic Change:** Modify the array sorting function. If using `Array.prototype.sort()`, swap the comparison operands.
- **DOM Change:** Inject the `data-testid` attribute into the JSX button element.

### 3. Scrum Master (SM)
**Sprint Task:**
- **Task ID:** `TASK-UI-001`
- **Title:** Invert Notification Sort & Add Test ID
- **Status:** In Progress

---

### 4. Developer (Implementation)

I am now applying the changes to `NotificationsList.tsx`.

```typescript
// src/components/NotificationsList.tsx (Partial view of changes)

// ... existing imports

export const NotificationsList = ({ notifications, onClearAll }) => {
  // 1. Invert sorting logic: b.timestamp - a.timestamp for Descending
  const sortedNotifications = [...notifications].sort((a, b) => {
    return new Date(b.timestamp).getTime() - new Date(a.timestamp).getTime();
  });

  return (
    <div className="notifications-container">
      <div className="header">
        <h3>Notifications</h3>
        {/* 2. Add data-testid to the clear button */}
        <button 
          onClick={onClearAll} 
          data-testid="clear-all-btn"
          className="clear-btn"
        >
          Clear All
        </button>
      </div>

      <ul>
        {sortedNotifications.map(notification => (
          <NotificationItem key={notification.id} data={notification} />
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  );
};
```

